ADDENDA <Act No. 18816, Feb. 3, 2022>
Article 1 (Enforcement date)
This Act shall enter into force six months after the date of its promulgation.
Article 2 (Preparation for establishment of the Korea Institute of Patent Information)
(1) The Commissioner of the Korean Intellectual Property Office shall commission up to seven establishing members, including the chairperson, from among those with knowledge of and experience in the field of informatization of industrial property rights and utilization of information to organize an establishment committee within 30 days from the date of promulgation of this Act, in order to have them conduct the administrative affairs regarding the establishment of the KIPI.
(2) The establishment committee shall prepare the following and obtain authorization thereof from the Commissioner of the Korean Intellectual Property Office:
1. The articles of incorporation of the KIPI;
2. A plan for the following matters succeeded to by the KIPI:
(a) Disposal of the claims, liabilities, other rights and obligations, and property of the Korea Institute of Patent Information established as an incorporated foundation under Article 32 of the Civil Act (hereinafter referred to as the "Korea Institute of Patent Information as an incorporated foundation") as at the time this Act enters into force;
(b) Succession to the employees of the Korea Institute of Patent Information as an incorporated foundation.
(3) The Commissioner of the Korean Intellectual Property Office shall appoint the first CEO, directors, and auditors of the KIPI upon recommendation of the establishment committee.
(4) Where the establishment committee obtains authorization under paragraph (2), it shall, without delay, register the establishment of the KIPI and transfer its administrative affairs to the head of the KIPI.
(5) The establishment committee and establishing members shall be deemed dissolved and dismissed when the transfer of administrative affairs under paragraph (4) is completed.
(6) The establishment of the KIPI may be subsidized by the budget of the Korea Institute of Patent Information as an incorporated foundation.
Article 3 (Transitional measures concerning establishment of the Korea Institute of Patent Information)
(1) The KIPI shall succeed to all rights, obligations, property, and employees of the Korea Institute of Patent Information as an incorporated foundation in accordance with the details of a plan authorized by the Commissioner of the Korean Intellectual Property Office pursuant to Article 2 (2) 2 of these Addenda.
(2) The value of the property to be succeeded to by the KIPI shall be the book value as of the day immediately preceding the registration of its establishment.
(3) The name of the Korea Institute of Patent Information as an incorporated foundation stated in the register or other public records as at the time this Act enters into force shall be deemed the name of the KIPI in accordance with the details of a plan authorized by the Commissioner of the Korean Intellectual Property Office pursuant to Article 2 (2) 2 of these Addenda.
(4) Any act done by or against the Korea Institute of Patent Information as an incorporated foundation before this Act enters into force shall be deemed an act done by or against KIPI in accordance with the details of a plan authorized by the Commissioner of the Korean Intellectual Property Office pursuant to Article 2 (2) 2 of these Addenda.
Article 4 (Transitional measures concerning designation of public institutions)  
The Korea Institute of Patent Information as an incorporated foundation designated as a public institution by the Minister of Economy and Finance under the Act on the Management of Public Institutions as at the time this Act enters into force shall be deemed the KIPI designated under this Act.

